{
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "c04-title-01",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter four. On a preposition.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-01",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A pronoun after a preposition is jarr, like any word after a preposition.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-02",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is fixed, so it is in the place of jarr.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-03",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pen is yours. That is, for you.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:1",
    "ex:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-04",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "القَلَمُ لَكَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:القَلَمُ لَكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-05",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for you, one man, comes after the preposition meaning for.",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": [
    "note:0",
    "ar:ـكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-06",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "That preposition is only one letter.",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-07",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun is in the place of jarr.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-08",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "He went out of it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-09",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "خَرَجَ مِنْهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:خَرَجَ مِنْهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-10",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun for it comes after the preposition meaning from.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:1",
    "ar:ـهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-11",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنْ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-12",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is in the place of jarr too.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-13",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The book is on it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-14",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الكِتَابُ عَلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:الكِتَابُ عَلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-15",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here the pronoun for it comes after the preposition meaning on.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:2",
    "ar:ـهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-16",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَى",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-prep-17",
   "scene": "c04-prep",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is in the place of jarr. Its kasra is not a sign of jarr. Only the sound changes. Chapter five explains it.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-01",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Some prepositions change their shape. Learn these forms.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-02",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Each row has the preposition, then the preposition with the pronoun for he, for you, and for me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-03",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In. In it, in you, in me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-04",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِي",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-05",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِيهِ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِيهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-06",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِيكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِيكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-07",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِيَّ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:فِيَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-08",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "On. On it, on you, on me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-09",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَى",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-10",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-11",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيْكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-12",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيَّ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-13",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "To. To it, to you, to me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-14",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَى",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-15",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-16",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَيْكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيْكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-17",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَيَّ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-18",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "From. From it, from you, from me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-19",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنْ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنْ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-20",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنْهُ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنْهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-21",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنْكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنْكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-22",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مِنِّي",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:مِنِّي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-23",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "For. This one is a single letter. For him, for you, for me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:4",
    "ar:لِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-24",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَهُ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-25",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-forms-26",
   "scene": "c04-forms",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لِي",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لِي"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-01",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Three changes to remember.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "b:0",
    "hl:Three changes to remember"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-02",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "One. The preposition meaning on.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-03",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَى",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-04",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Before a pronoun, its end changes to this shape.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْـ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-05",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "On it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-06",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَيْهِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:عَلَيْهِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-07",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Two. The preposition meaning to.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-08",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَى",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَى"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-09",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Its end changes in the same way.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيْـ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-10",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "To her.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-11",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "إِلَيْهَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:إِلَيْهَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-12",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Three. The preposition meaning for is one letter with a kasra.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لِ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-13",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Before a pronoun, it takes a fatha.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-14",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "For him, for you, for her.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-15",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَهُ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَهُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-16",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَكَ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَكَ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-17",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لَهَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لَهَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-18",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Only with the pronoun for me does it keep its kasra. For me.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:ـي",
    "hl:it stays"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-19",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "لِي",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:لِي"
   ]
  }
 ]
}